(7597652, 1226429, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment.<br/> <br/>It is a good shot and very colorful but with the flat black backdrop there is no visual cue that the viewer is looking at the glasses from below. The angle could be an overhead view looking down....no definitive way to tell for sure. Which is why I think it needs that visual cue. I.E. if there was the backdrop of a blue sky with clouds perhaps even lined up to look like they are spilling out from the glasses it would definitely give an instant clue of looking up from underneath.</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment. It is a good shot and very colorful but with the flat black backdrop there is no visual cue that the viewer is looking at the glasses from below. The angle could be an overhead view looking down....no definitive way to tell for sure. Which is why I think it needs that visual cue. I.E. if there was the backdrop of a blue sky with clouds perhaps even lined up to look like they are spilling out from the glasses it would definitely give an instant clue of looking up from underneath.', '2018-09-25 23:19:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(7597653, 1226281, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment.<br/> <br/>The Milky way and a sky full of stars is definitely breathtaking to behold! Love the orientation that has the Milky Way cross the frame at a diagonal. Wonderful capture! My only critique is that I think the night sky looks just a tad washed out and can use a adjustment to the contrast to make it a bit darker.</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment. The Milky way and a sky full of stars is definitely breathtaking to behold! Love the orientation that has the Milky Way cross the frame at a diagonal. Wonderful capture! My only critique is that I think the night sky looks just a tad washed out and can use a adjustment to the contrast to make it a bit darker.', '2018-09-25 23:24:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(7597654, 1226435, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment.<br/> <br/>The perspective of looking up and seeing the barbed wire and spikes of the gates in this city street with the buildings looming high above makes one question how they feel at this particular spot. Does it give a sense of the security or does it make one feel imprisoned within these tall walls? That is a question that is up to the viewer as to how they perceive this. A good photo with an interesting perspective that makes one stop and think.</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment. The perspective of looking up and seeing the barbed wire and spikes of the gates in this city street with the buildings looming high above makes one question how they feel at this particular spot. Does it give a sense of the security or does it make one feel imprisoned within these tall walls? That is a question that is up to the viewer as to how they perceive this. A good photo with an interesting perspective that makes one stop and think.', '2018-09-25 23:31:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(7597655, 1226432, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment.<br/> <br/>I love umbrellas and this colorful art installation is beautiful to look upon! It is a good shot but needs something ''more'' to make it a stand out shot. As is it is a straight on shot with the umbrellas lined up neatly in straight rows. It just needs some oomph to put some added visual interest into a static shot. The only two things that I can suggest. One is to have taken it where the umbrellas run at a diagonal. The other is from a low angle looking up to capture a person''s face in the corner and their hand reaching up as if to grab hold of an umbrella.</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment. I love umbrellas and this colorful art installation is beautiful to look upon! It is a good shot but needs something ''more'' to make it a stand out shot. As is it is a straight on shot with the umbrellas lined up neatly in straight rows. It just needs some oomph to put some added visual interest into a static shot. The only two things that I can suggest. One is to have taken it where the umbrellas run at a diagonal. The other is from a low angle looking up to capture a person''s face in the corner and their hand reaching up as if to grab hold of an umbrella.', '2018-09-25 23:41:50.000000', NULL, 1),
